 "logline": "Four days before the ashes: a feast for the sick, a torch on a kitchen television, a parade in their own neighborhood, red envelopes in the East, and a king on St. Charles — and nobody is supposed to do anything for Laney’s birthday.",
 "previously": [
  {
   "text": "On Esplanade at a quarter to four in the morning, Lena: “I wanted you here for this,” … “Since September.”"
  },
  {
   "text": "In the front room, Mémère: “You receive in the hand,” … “Left over the right, like a throne. Somebody taught you.”",
   "if": "went_up_holy_rosary && !absolution_withheld"
  },
  {
   "text": "In the front room, Mémère: “You stayed in the pew Sunday. Lucien noticed.”",
   "if": "!went_up_holy_rosary || absolution_withheld"
  },
  {
   "text": "On the phone from Burnaby, Skye: “That’s the problem with being good,” … “Nobody can tell.”"
  },
  {
   "text": "On the Magnolia Bridge, Lena: “Well,” … “I didn’t ask.” — You: “You didn’t have to.”",
   "if": "said_didnt_have_to"
  },
  {
   "text": "On the Magnolia Bridge, Lena: “Well,” … “I didn’t ask.”",
   "if": "!said_didnt_have_to"
  },
  {
